# checkout

**Verdict: INFEASIBLE.** 99.95% is not possible: even if everything you own were perfect, dependencies cap you at 99.93%. Add redundancy to the dependencies or promise the 99.90% tier.

| | Availability | Downtime per window |
|---|---|---|
| Target | 99.95% | 21.6 min |
| Computed | 99.91% | 38.9 min |
| Dependency ceiling | 99.93% | 30.3 min |

Recommended tier: **99.90%**. Window: 30 days.

## Biggest levers

| Component | Availability | Gain if made perfect |
|---|---|---|
| auth | 99.95% | +0.0500 pp |
| payments | 99.90% | +0.0200 pp |
| self | 99.98% | +0.0200 pp |
| db-primary | 99.95% | +0.0000 pp |
| db-replica | 99.95% | +0.0000 pp |

## Single points of failure

- payments
- auth
- self

## Pairs that take it down together

- db-primary + db-replica
- az-a + db-replica
- db-primary + az-b
- az-a + az-b

## Warnings

- payments is a single point of failure at 99.90%, below the 99.95% target
